<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    A LaunchAgent for the opening-bell run. macOS only; see docs/scheduling.md.

    The third of three, and the last piece of a weekday that looks like this on
    Pacific time:

        06:30  com.stonksmith.morning   renders the brief on last night's close
        06:35  com.stonksmith.open      scrapes, five minutes after the open
        18:30  com.stonksmith.nightly   scrapes, after TSP has published

    Ten scrapes a week rather than five. The five minute gap after the brief is
    load-bearing: the brief reads every database in the workspace and this one
    writes them, so firing them together would have the brief reporting on a
    workspace caught mid-write.

    The close run stays at 18:30 rather than moving to the 13:00 bell, and that
    is deliberate. TSP publishes the day's share prices in the evening, so a
    13:00 run would record yesterday's price as today's, every day, with nothing
    saying so. 18:30 local is 21:30 Eastern here, comfortably past it.

    Two values below have to be edited, the same two every agent in this
    directory needs. There is no way for a committed file to know either.

      ProgramArguments   the absolute path to scripts/stonksmith-open.sh in your
                         checkout. The script finds the repository from its own
                         location, so this is the only path to set.

      PATH               must contain uv. `which uv` says where yours is; uv's
                         installer puts it in ~/.local/bin, which is not in the
                         list below, and launchd does no tilde expansion here.

    Install, from the repository:

        mkdir -p ~/Library/LaunchAgents
        sed "s|/PATH/TO/StonkSmith|$PWD|; s|^\(.*<string>\)/usr/local/bin|\1$(dirname "$(command -v uv)"):/usr/local/bin|" \
            scripts/com.stonksmith.open.plist > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.stonksmith.open.plist
        launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.stonksmith.open.plist

    `launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.stonksmith.open` removes it, and
    `launchctl kickstart -p gui/$(id -u)/com.stonksmith.open` runs it now rather
    than waiting for the morning, which is how to test it.

    gui/$(id -u) rather than `launchctl load` is the point of the whole file, as
    it is for the nightly agent: it bootstraps into the GUI login session, which
    is the context that can read the login keychain. SnapTrade and Schwab 529
    both resolve a secret from there, and a keyring lookup outside that session
    returns empty rather than erroring, so a system-level agent would report a
    missing consumer key and a failed login rather than a permissions problem.

    StartCalendarInterval fires on wake if the machine was asleep at the time.
    A laptop shut at 06:35 is the ordinary case, not the exception.

    One caveat this file cannot repeat often enough, and the runner spells out
    at length: only SnapTrade carries new information at the open. TSP, the 529
    and Ally all rest on a published close that does not exist yet at 06:35, so
    their 06:35 marks repeat yesterday's numbers under a new timestamp. They
    report their own as_of honestly, and reading a morning price into them is
    the mistake to avoid.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.stonksmith.open</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>/PATH/TO/StonkSmith/scripts/stonksmith-open.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- Weekdays, five minutes after the 06:30 Pacific open and five minutes
         after the brief. Weekday 1 is Monday; 0 and 7 are both Sunday. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/stonksmith-open.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/stonksmith-open.log</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
